& [ActivationIdentity] is bounded Phase 2 implementation authority
  + [canonical_specification_uuid] is 4090fcfc-b61d-41d4-896e-c9eb88d82409
  + [profile] is cantor-read-only-live-codex/0.1
  + [conversation_uuid] is cab190f5-eda0-44e0-81a5-51f9605e0baa
  + [status] is authorized_for_one_live_read_only_turn_profile
  + [semantic_authority] remains verified cantor_core ProtocolResponse
  + [agent_authority] is one ephemeral Codex thread and one turn
  + [process_authority] is exact Codex app-server and exact cantor-mcp child only
  + [filesystem_authority] is read_only
  + [network_authority] is false inside the turn
  + [effect_authority] is none

& [LiveCodexConfig] is operator-explicit immutable input
  + [profile] is cantor-live-codex-config/0.1
  + [codex_executable] is canonical absolute regular non-symlink path
  + [codex_executable_sha256] is expected lowercase SHA-256
  + [codex_version] is exact expected bounded version output
  + [cantor_mcp_executable] is canonical absolute regular non-symlink path
  + [cantor_mcp_executable_sha256] is expected lowercase SHA-256
  + [environment_path] is canonical absolute regular non-symlink path
  + [environment_sha256] is expected lowercase SHA-256
  + [working_directory] is canonical absolute directory
  + [server_name] is the exact nonreserved MCP server name
  + [tool_name] is query_sop
  + [timeout_milliseconds] is positive and bounded
  + [maximum_line_bytes] is positive and bounded
  + [maximum_events] is positive and bounded
  + [maximum_total_bytes] is positive and bounded
  = must: validate and hash every path before process launch
  - never: discover, copy, serialize, or log Codex credentials

& [AppServerProtocol] is stable stdio JSONL
  + [launch] is exact Codex executable with app-server and stable config overrides
  + [transport] is piped stdin and stdout with separately drained bounded stderr
  + [request_ids] are deterministic unique positive integers
  + [initialize] supplies Cantor client name, title, and version without experimentalApi
  + [initialized] follows only a successful initialize response
  + [responses] must match one outstanding request id and contain result without error
  + [notifications] are admitted only by method and typed parameters
  + [server_requests] are unexpected and fail the profile
  = must: reject malformed, oversized, duplicate, unknown-response, or premature messages

& [ReadOnlyThread] is nonpersistent least authority
  + [thread_start] sets ephemeral true, exact cwd, approvalPolicy never, sandbox read-only, and Cantor service name
  + [thread_response] supplies one nonempty exact thread id
  + [MCP_readiness] is required by app-server configuration and thread start fails if Cantor MCP cannot initialize
  + [experimental_fields] are absent
  - never: resume, fork, name, archive, persist, inject items, compact, roll back, or mutate metadata

& [SingleTurn] is one bounded assignment
  + [turn_start] names the exact thread id and one text input
  + [sandboxPolicy] is readOnly with networkAccess false
  + [approvalPolicy] is never
  + [outputSchema] is a closed JSON object for summary, satisfied criterion identifiers, proof identifiers, and requested effects
  + [model] is omitted so operator Codex configuration selects it
  + [turn_response] supplies one nonempty exact turn id and inProgress state
  - never: steer, retry, interrupt except timeout cleanup, invoke a skill, or provide an image

& [AssignmentPrimer] is concise semantic control
  + [identity] is exact commission, work packet, frame, subject, purpose, and requested result
  + [authority] is exact allowed MCP server and tool with no other tool authority
  + [request] is canonical JSON ProtocolRequest supplied as untrusted tool arguments to reproduce exactly
  + [criteria] are exact work-packet identifiers and descriptions
  + [proof] requires declared proof identifiers to be preserved
  + [instruction] is call the Cantor tool exactly once then return only the schema-bound candidate
  - never: ask Codex to inspect files, run commands, browse, write, or reason from unsigned semantic text instead of the tool result

& [EventAdmission] is an immutable bounded observation ledger
  + [allowed_notifications] are thread/started, thread/status/changed, turn/started, item/started, item/completed, item/agentMessage/delta, thread/tokenUsage/updated, warning, and turn/completed
  + [required_item_1] is one completed mcpToolCall with exact server and query_sop tool
  + [required_item_2] is one completed agentMessage with phase final_answer or absent legacy phase
  + [terminal] is turn/completed for the exact turn with completed status
  + [budgets] are timeout, line bytes, total bytes, and event count
  + [ordering] is tool completion before final agent completion before terminal turn completion
  = must: retain digests and typed summary for every admitted event
  + [commentary] is passive and cannot substitute for the one final candidate
  + [set_semantics] is enforced after strict JSON parsing because the provider strict-schema subset does not admit uniqueItems

& [ForbiddenEventSet] is no hidden authority
  + [forbidden_item] is commandExecution, fileChange, webSearch, dynamicToolCall, collabAgentToolCall, imageGeneration, or any unknown actionable item
  + [forbidden_request] is approval, permission, user input, MCP elicitation, dynamic tool callback, attestation, or unknown server request
  + [forbidden_state] is second tool call, second final message, other server, other tool, failed item, interrupted turn, or failed turn
  = must: fault immediately and preserve the accepted observation prefix

& [MCPTranslation] is exact Cantor evidence
  + [arguments] decode as strict ProtocolRequest equal to the commissioned expected request
  + [result] yields one strict ProtocolResponse
  + [verification] is cantor_core verify_protocol_response plus Success status
  + [identity] is exact request id, operation, expected environment digest, expected package set, scope, and caller context
  - never: reconstruct a missing field from agent prose or trust the agent summary instead of tool result

& [CandidateTranslation] is schema-bound untrusted output
  + [summary] is bounded nonempty text
  + [satisfied_criterion_ids] is a bounded set of known SemanticIds
  + [proof_refs] is a bounded set of SemanticIds exactly equal to the supervisor-admitted proof set
  + [requested_effects] must be returned without suppression
  + [content_digest] is SHA-256 of exact final agent-message UTF-8 bytes
  + [candidate_uuid] is deterministically derived from the work packet and turn identity
  = must: pass CandidateArtifact validation before ecosystem append

& [EcosystemBridge] is logical replay of observed physical events
  + [CodexAdapter] performs the one live turn when accepting the assignment and buffers the immutable observed request, response, and candidate
  + [ObservedCantorAdapter] exposes only the exact buffered ProtocolResponse when the ecosystem requests the matching ProtocolRequest
  + [CodexAdapter] releases the candidate only when the ecosystem returns that exact response
  + [runtime] remains the existing seven-message run_supervised_mock_cycle and deterministic Observer
  = must: preserve query then return then candidate logical order even though the completed app-server turn is buffered before translation
  - never: claim the buffer changes causal order inside Codex inference

& [ProcessLifecycle] is bounded cleanup
  + [normal] is close stdin after terminal completion and wait briefly for app-server shutdown
  + [timeout_or_fault] is close stdin, request exact child kill if still live, wait, and return typed fault
  + [stderr] is concurrently drained to a bounded buffer and discarded without entering protocol evidence or logs
  + [MCP_child] is owned and reaped by app-server
  - never: kill by PID without the exact Child handle or leave a detached process

& [RequirementSet] is traceable
  + [RLC-001] is source-selected SJS authority after passed mock prerequisite
  + [RLC-002] is exact executable, environment, path, digest, version, and runtime configuration admission
  + [RLC-003] is strict initialized app-server JSONL request and response protocol
  + [RLC-004] is one ephemeral read-only approval-never thread
  + [RLC-005] is one read-only no-network schema-bound turn
  + [RLC-006] is one exact stable Cantor MCP query_sop call
  + [RLC-007] is bounded correlated event ordering and completion
  + [RLC-008] is fail-closed forbidden action, request, and state rejection
  + [RLC-009] is exact ProtocolRequest and verified ProtocolResponse translation
  + [RLC-010] is schema-bound CandidateArtifact and existing ecosystem bridge
  + [RLC-011] is deterministic fake-server proof plus one explicit live fingerprinted proof
  + [RLC-012] is no write, steering, retry, persistence, dynamic tool, manager iteration, notification, multi-worker, or effect authority

& [Verification] is layered
  + [unit] is configuration, path, digest, version, JSONL, identity, budget, event, tool, candidate, and cleanup tests
  + [fake_integration] is a deterministic scripted app-server transcript proving emitted request order and every material negative gate
  + [live_integration] is explicit operator-supplied paths and digests against one actual ephemeral read-only turn
  + [live_acceptance] is exactly one successful Cantor call, zero forbidden actions, verified response, accepted Observer decision, and complete process cleanup
  + [global] is format, warnings-denied lint, debug and overflow-checked release tests, release build, docs, dependency audit, evidence, fault, and Git proof

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is seven-fold
  + [fold_1] is phase_2 source selection and passed Phase 1 prerequisite
  + [fold_2] is stable app-server control versus stable MCP tool versus deferred experimental dynamic tools
  + [fold_3] is exact configuration, JSON-RPC, event, MCP, candidate, and evidence data
  + [fold_4] is handshake, thread, turn, event, tool, and cleanup state machines
  + [fold_5] is executable, credential, sandbox, approval, network, tool, and effect security
  + [fold_6] is malformed, reordered, substituted, oversized, timed-out, interrupted, failed, and hidden-action faults
  + [fold_7] is deterministic fake proof before one explicit fingerprinted live proof with every later phase locked

